# Blueprint

## Current game reality
The current game is `100 Clicks Cat`, a single-screen timed tap-target/clicker arcade game. The player starts from a title card, taps/clicks a large cat target on a Canvas playfield, gains exactly +1 progress per successful hit, the cat relocates after each hit, and victory occurs at 100 successful taps. The HUD shows progress out of 100 and elapsed time. There is no enemy hazard, health, lives, fail state, or explicit level system; the only pressure is speed, target acquisition, spatial retargeting after each click, and the final completion time. Rendering is Canvas-based with DOM overlay UI, reaction badges/GIFs, particles, remote catalog-style audio, and mouse/touch input.

## High-level code structure
The game is implemented in `index.html` with embedded CSS and JavaScript. It uses a full-screen Canvas for animated background, cat target, and particles; DOM overlays for start/victory screens, HUD, reaction badge, and reaction GIFs; an AudioController for BGM, SFX, and victory loops; and requestAnimationFrame for rendering while active or particles remain.

## Game loop / state model
DOMContentLoaded initializes assets, Canvas, audio, state, and event handlers. Start unlocks audio, hides the start panel, shows HUD, centers the cat, resets score/timer, and starts the requestAnimationFrame loop. Each successful tap increments score, plays feedback, spawns particles, optionally shows milestone feedback, relocates the cat, and updates HUD. At 100 taps, play stops, final time is shown, victory UI appears, victory audio/particles play, and restart returns to the startable loop.

## Player goals
Tap/click the moving cat target 100 times as quickly as possible; the score is completion progress and the timer is a performance metric.

## Interaction pattern
Touchstart and click/mouse-style pointer events map to a coordinate check against the cat target. There is no keyboard movement or drag control.

